1|//! The closed telemetry classes (0.6.1 parity): the vendor table, the closed model lists, the
2|//! coordinator ("judge") classifier of a rating event and the `consult_ref` of a ledger entry.
3|//!
4|//! A port of the plugin's `$script:TelemetryVendors`, `Get-TelemetryVendorByHost`,
5|//! `Get-TelemetryModelToken`, `Get-TelemetryJudgeClass`, `Find-TelemetryRosterEntry`,
6|//! `Get-TelemetryRosterVendor`, `Test-TelemetryCoordinatorNamed`, `Get-TelemetryRatingActor`,
7|//! `Resolve-TelemetryJudge`, `ConvertTo-TelemetryJudge` and `Get-TelemetryConsultRef`
8|//! (`codex-consult-common.ps1` at v0.6.1). Privacy by construction: every value these functions
9|//! return is the TABLE's own text (a vendor class, an entry of that class's model list) or one of
10|//! the fixed words `other` / `unknown` - never a roster label, a host, or a model as the operator
11|//! typed it. The ledger and every local file keep the real ones.
